---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site, hasContact } from "../site";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use · Centre Pullz"
  description="Terms for using Centre Pullz: what the measurements are, what they are not, attribution and image rights, and the limits of the play advice published here."
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {site.legalUpdated}</p>
    <p class="lede">
      By using Centre Pullz you accept the terms below. They're short and written
      to be read.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      A free, informational reference about the weight distribution of crane-game
      prize boxes. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, for
      general information only.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy — please read this one</h2>
    <p>
      The measurements are transcribed from public posts by a third party and
      describe <em>the specific box that person measured</em>. The source posts
      themselves state that prizes vary between individual units depending on how
      the figure was packed. Transcription and translation errors are also
      possible.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing here is a guarantee about the prize in front of you. Machine
      settings — claw strength, bar spacing, prize placement, payout
      configuration — are controlled by the arcade operator and are not reflected
      in this data.
    </p>

    <h2>The play tips are AI-generated</h2>
    <p>
      Each entry ends with a suggested approach produced by an AI model reading
      that entry's measurements. They are labelled as such on every page. They are
      opinion and inference, not expert advice, and may be wrong. Use your own
      judgement.
    </p>

    <h2>Spending</h2>
    <p>
      Crane games cost money and are configured so that, on average, players spend
      more than the prize is worth. This site may improve your understanding of a
      machine; it does not make playing profitable and does not predict outcomes.
      You are solely responsible for what you choose to spend. Set a limit before
      you play. If gambling or arcade spending is causing you harm, please seek
      local support services.
    </p>

    <h2>Attribution and source data</h2>
    <p>
      All measurements originate with
      <a href={site.sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Merry☆An ({site.sourceHandle})</a>
      and every entry links to the original post. This site is not affiliated
      with, endorsed by, or operated in partnership with Merry☆An.
    </p>

    <h2>Trademarks and images</h2>
    <p>
      Prize names, series names, character names and manufacturer names are the
      trademarks of their respective owners. Centre Pullz is not affiliated with,
      endorsed by, or sponsored by Banpresto, Bandai Spirits, Furyu, Sega, Taito,
      or any other rights holder, arcade operator or publisher named on this site.
      Names are used descriptively to identify the prize being measured.
    </p>
    <p>
      Product photographs are displayed directly from the manufacturers' own
      servers and remain their property; they are not copied or re-hosted here.
      Measurement diagrams are the photographer's own work and are credited.
    </p>

    <h2>Takedown requests</h2>
    <p>
      If you hold rights to material shown here and want it removed, contact us
      with the page URL and the material in question and it will be taken down
      while the request is reviewed.
    </p>

    <h2>Using our content</h2>
    <p>
      You're welcome to read, link to, and reference this site. Please don't
      scrape it wholesale to republish as your own database — link to the entry
      instead, and credit the original measurements to Merry☆An.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, Centre Pullz and its operator are
      not liable for any loss — including money spent on arcade machines — arising
      from use of, or reliance on, this site. Some jurisdictions do not allow
      certain exclusions, so parts of this section may not apply to you.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated; the "last updated" date above will change when
      they are. Continuing to use the site means accepting the current version.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    {hasContact ? (
      <p>
        Questions or takedown requests: <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p class="mono note">A contact method for this site has not been published yet.</p>
    )}
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .note {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
